{"title":"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3a","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Listing)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Listing)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Faster)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Blocks_of_4_Integers)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Blocks of 4 Integers)</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2019 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 3\">Problem 3</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Tania lists the positive integers, in order, leaving out the integers that are multiples of 5. Her resulting list is\n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/8/0/180a87fead2ec0eeedbccea40a86c0058976c34f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"321\" height=\"17\" /></center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>How many integers has Tania listed just before she leaves out the 6th multiple of 5?\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Listing.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Listing)\">Solution 1 (Listing)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Listing)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Listing all of the numbers before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/b/a/3baf0066ce7886d39f68ef8e6ac40747eaf9ca6d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 5 = 30$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"85\" height=\"15\" /> that aren't left out, we get:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/6/7/16715099a149bdefa8ea061ec16b25d11df1087e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 3, 4, 6, 7, 8, 9, 11, 12, 13, 14, 16, 17, 18, 19, 21, 22, 23, 24, 26, 27, 28, 29$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"551\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p>Counting, we see that there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d2cca89d5aa7ed0a9130ce403b8bf8a23a869c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"30\" height=\"23\" /> numbers.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Faster.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Faster)\">Solution 2 (Faster)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Faster)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that before <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/a/60a7625aaac7264acd616bcefca1d92a1b9a35e0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"42\" height=\"15\" />, Tania leaves out <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/0/79069377f91364c2f87a64e5f9f562a091c8a6c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$5$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers. There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/6/5/0657f5cd42256c0a39d45b265235e2a939625515.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29$\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> in total, so she must have listed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/8/8f8d806b2bc11358f2340fad197351ac8b5531e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$29 - 5 = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"105\" height=\"25\" /> numbers.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Blocks_of_4_Integers.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Blocks_of_4_Integers)\">Solution 3 (Blocks of 4 Integers)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3a&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Blocks of 4 Integers)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We can realize that there would be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> blocks of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> integers because there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/c/c7cab1a05e1e0c1d51a6a219d96577a16b7abf9d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> numbers before another number is left out. Thus, she must have listed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/8/6/c8622bef477b7f77bff99e25f43ae804b79b337f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 \\times 4 = \\boxed{24}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"96\" height=\"25\" /> numbers.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018011045\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.016 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.040 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 76/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 245/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2553/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    6.621      1 2019_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_3\n100.00%    6.621      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36931:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018011045 and revision id 285737. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}